WEBVTT

00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:37.100
Nishi...

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:40.540
Hey, old man, pick up the pace!

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:42.370
I feel like I've become a pro boxer already!

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:45.720
Idiot, save that for after you've taken the exam!

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:47.500
C'mon, I've come this far, so I've practically passed!

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:50.810
I'm gonna beat up that examiner!

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:52.480
Hey, Nishi!

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:53.460
Y-Yes, Coach!

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:57.670
Now that we've made it here, you'd better give it your all! Remember that!

00:01:57.670 --> 00:01:58.970
O-Okay, understood!

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:03.060
Geez! One of them's too excited, and the other's too nervous...

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:04.940
I sure hope nothing goes wrong...

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:39.250
Yahoo, they're all here, they're all here!

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.470
Yo!

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:42.970
Hey!

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:43.820
Yo!

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:45.220
Get it, get in!

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:46.810
Here we go.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:50.150
Hey, big guy, are you a heavyweight?

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:53.150
Isn't it obvious? Now keep it down!

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:55.590
So you're a heavyweight after all!

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:57.150
Hey Nishi, come here for a bit!

00:02:57.870 --> 00:02:59.020
Come here for a second.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:03.080
This guy is in the heavyweight class, just like you.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:05.660
Come here and greet him. You might face him in the ring.

00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:09.160
A-Allow me to introduce myself. My name is Nishi. Pleased to meet you!

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:12.770
S-Same here, my name is—

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:15.630
Hey, man, don't be so stiff! This ain't an arranged marriage!

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:18.560
Your body's in great shape as I would expect!

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:22.640
Dammit! What's this idiot thinking, getting all cocky!?

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:26.640
Sorry for the delay, we shall begin the test now.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:31.630
We request that chairmen and spectators wait in the lobby.

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:34.150
Those of you taking the test, come this way.

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:36.770
Yeah, hurry up and go!

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:40.770
Yo! You just wait, old man!

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:42.160
I'm gonna go kick some ass!

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:43.160
Hey, hurry up, hurry up!

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:47.120
Here we go.

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:54.240
Both of you...

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:56.600
Both of you, do your best!

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:00.960
Here!

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:02.720
Take a seat once you get a number.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.900
Hey, Nishi, your digits add up to nine!

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:12.690
Mine adds up to eight!

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:15.190
It's our lucky day.

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:18.690
What's with the pale face? Come on.

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:20.570
You don't need to sweat yourself over this test.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:22.840
I'm here with you afterall!

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:26.120
Yabuki-kun, you sure are excited, aren't you?

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:28.960
Oh, if it isn't Inagaki! I didn't expect to see you here!

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:31.180
Hey, Nishi, it's Inagaki.

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:33.210
The national high-school champ.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:34.130
N-Nice to meet you.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:38.090
I don't mean to pry, but will you really be all right?

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:39.070
What do you mean?

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:40.350
I am talking about you.

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:45.090
Given the way you were sparring, you should think this over. The road to pro boxing is tough, you know.

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:49.220
And here I was wondering what you were gonna say... "Shut up, or I'll hit you!"

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:52.230
I am just saying this for your sake, you know.

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:55.950
Did you hear that, Nishi?

00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:57.210
"For your sake," he says!

00:04:57.210 --> 00:04:59.180
Then let me tell you something "for your sake"!

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:01.890
Do you really think your punch is at pro-level?

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:04.240
Your student discount cards won't apply here!

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:07.430
You're better off bringing your lunchbox to school than being here.

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:08.200
How 'bout that?

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:11.240
Hey, quiet now! Quiet!

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:16.150
Allow me to say this before we begin the test.

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:21.250
In order to make the gradings fair, we'll be calling you by your test registration numbers.

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:25.260
In other words, any personal connections to the judges will have no effect on the decision.

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:28.220
Great! That's the way it should be!

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:29.720
It's a world determined by skills only.

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:31.690
Silence!

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:35.730
The main purpose of this test is health management.

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:39.760
Boxing has a high risk aspect.

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:42.910
Those who can't withstand the furious battle will unmistakably fail.

00:05:42.910 --> 00:05:48.710
Thus, it's not just your body that is put under the test, but your mind and technique as well!

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:51.290
Well then, I'll be handing out the written test now.

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:52.700
Keep them face down.

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:55.720
W-Written test?

00:05:56.510 --> 00:05:57.680
Wait, does he mean with a pencil...?

00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:58.750
Of course!

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:01.920
This is weird.

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:05.050
If this is a boxing test, shouldn't we be punching each other?

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:06.760
Here, take a sheet and pass the rest around.

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:08.730
What are you saying now?

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:12.760
Didn't you just nod when he said boxing isn't all about the body?

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:15.290
Don't look yet!

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:18.770
How can you remain so calm?

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:20.190
No, not really.

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:21.780
I'm not that calm.

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:25.920
You're pretty sharp for someone with a dumb face.

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:26.780
Isn't that great?

00:06:29.870 --> 00:06:31.320
Well, well, don't mind me!

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:33.550
I'm calm now that you're sitting beside me.

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:34.870
I'll be counting on you!

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:40.600
Moreover, if anyone is caught cheating, they'll be immediately thrown out of the room,

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:43.920
and will be permanently prohibited from taking the test again.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:48.380
Such imprudence will not be accepted from a boxer.

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:53.260
All right, turn over your tests.

00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:55.420
You have fifty minutes.

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:55.980
Begin!

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:06.650
Damn it, I can't stay still.

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:10.680
I'd be more at ease if I took the test for Joe and Nishi.

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.940
Either way... Two more hours to go.

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:17.790
Don't lose your cool now, Danpei!

00:07:21.470 --> 00:07:24.300
Number 26, weighing in at 118 pounds. Bantamweight class.

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:26.030
Next!

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:31.800
Hey, Number 26!

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:34.260
Who told you to start practicing shadow boxing!?

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:36.510
All right, all right, I understand!

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:39.750
Geez, I'm not used to this at all!

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:42.660
Number 27, 179 pounds, heavyweight class.

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:43.560
All right, next!

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:46.430
Joe, how was your written exam?

00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:50.590
I thought some math or English questions would show up.

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:51.870
But what do you know?

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:53.570
It was just questions related to boxing!

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:57.100
It was so easy, I finished with time to spare!

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:58.410
So then, Joe...

00:07:59.570 --> 00:08:03.710
what did you write for the question regarding the three fouls in boxing?

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:05.590
Oh that!

00:08:06.110 --> 00:08:07.710
First, there is biting... right?

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:08.620
Then there is kicking, and tickling your opponent.

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:10.030
Then there is kicking, and tickling your opponent.

00:08:10.030 --> 00:08:11.130
Those are the correct answers.

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:13.910
I see. Tickling—

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:15.130
What!?

00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:17.560
W-Wait, is that what you really wrote!?

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:20.250
Wh-What's wrong?

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:23.560
Th-Those aren't the fouls!

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:24.560
Why not?

00:08:26.510 --> 00:08:29.680
Listen, Joe, the answer is...

00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:38.580
Holding your opponent's arms: hold.

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:40.080
Those three are the right answers.

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:41.630
Oh, man...

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:44.780
S-So the answers were that simple...

00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:47.050
Damn it, I made such a foolish mistake.

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:53.050
Well then, what did you write for the "three correct ways of defence" question?

00:08:53.780 --> 00:08:56.620
Ah, that I definitely nailed!

00:08:56.620 --> 00:08:58.060
I wrote down a superb answer!

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:04.150
There is no need for three ways of defence. In boxing there is only one way!

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:05.360
O-One!?

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:07.550
Did he say one...!?

00:09:07.550 --> 00:09:08.400
And it is?

00:09:08.930 --> 00:09:12.130
In other words: attack, attack and attack.

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:14.770
Attack is the best defence!

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:15.910
See?

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:19.410
Piece o' cake! Such an awesome answer, isn't it!?

00:09:23.070 --> 00:09:24.410
This is really bad!

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:30.240
What's wrong with you people!? What's so funny!?

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:31.500
What do you mean, "This is bad?"

00:09:31.770 --> 00:09:37.470
M-Maybe it's not all that bad, but in this case there are three right ways of defending.

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:47.880
Wrapping your arms around the opponent: clinch work.

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:49.110
Those are the three ways.

00:09:52.410 --> 00:09:54.140
Damn it!

00:09:54.140 --> 00:09:56.950
So many trick questions!

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:02.030
Now, now, don't get worked up over this...

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:03.820
Listen!

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:06.040
I definitely got the third question right.

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:10.000
"How many times can a boxer fall down in one round before he loses the match by TKO?"

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.510
So... What did you write for that one?

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:15.990
Please let us know.

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:18.690
I really want to hear the "right" answer!

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:22.200
All right, I'll tell you!

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:24.370
It doesn't matter how many times a boxer falls down!

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:25.810
If the referee counts till 10...

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:28.060
and he doesn't stand up...

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:30.060
he will lose by TKO.

00:10:37.890 --> 00:10:40.070
"It doesn't matter how many times," he says!

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:44.080
I've never heard that rule before!

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:51.040
Joe, I understand. You really are a man born to fight.

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:55.560
It is your innate fighting instinct that caused you to get all three questions wrong.

00:10:56.540 --> 00:10:57.590
Did I get this wrong too?

00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:59.090
Yabuki-kun.

00:10:59.810 --> 00:11:05.060
You lose if you go down three times in a single round. It's a basic rule in boxing.

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:06.670
He's a little crazy, isn't he?

00:11:06.670 --> 00:11:07.650
Look, Joe...

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:11.540
I don't blame you for not knowing.

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:15.290
You've been boxing without learning those rules.

00:11:15.290 --> 00:11:20.570
Just like in your fight with Rikiishi, it was, "It didn't matter how many times you fall down in one round."

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:23.590
"The one who knocks down his opponent for good, wins."

00:11:23.590 --> 00:11:25.550
That's what you thought.

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:32.230
Come to think about it...

00:11:32.230 --> 00:11:38.920
All the boxing you've done so far is recklessly rough, self-styled boxing.

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:41.310
Okay, I understand. Keep quiet now.

00:11:41.910 --> 00:11:45.680
Hey, I really think you should pick up a book and study boxing...

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:48.680
As if reading a book makes you stronger!

00:11:53.430 --> 00:11:56.690
So I got two or three questions wrong. That's no big deal!

00:11:56.690 --> 00:11:58.360
What are you talking about Joe?

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:00.700
The whole exam was only three questions!

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:03.930
Zero... Zero!

00:12:04.630 --> 00:12:06.700
You scored zero points! What are you going to do about it?

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:09.700
I know already, numbskull, just be quiet!

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:14.430
Shut up!

00:12:14.430 --> 00:12:17.210
Shut up already! Quit it with the irritating laughter!

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:18.230
It pisses me off!

00:12:19.220 --> 00:12:22.080
<i>Number 26 and Number 27!</i>

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:24.180
<i>Number 26 and Number 27!</i>

00:12:24.750 --> 00:12:27.260
<i>Please head to the office downstairs.</i>

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:28.910
Joe, it's me and you.

00:12:28.910 --> 00:12:29.850
I wonder what's up?

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:32.330
You can go home now, #1 reject!

00:12:32.330 --> 00:12:33.790
Congratulations!

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:37.050
Now get out of here!

00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:03.840
Um... I think I'll give up on the B class, like you suggested.

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:04.550
If it's not too hard...

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:06.700
I'll take the C class instead.

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:11.560
Number 27, changed to C class.

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:15.430
So much for registering you for the B class!

00:13:15.430 --> 00:13:17.400
Didn't I tell you before?

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:24.420
That famous Sakurai Takao, who fought in the Tokyo Olympics, got the B class license just recently.

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:27.530
It's reckless for us to challenge the B class at this stage.

00:13:29.230 --> 00:13:32.250
Do as you please, throwing people's concern for you away.

00:13:32.250 --> 00:13:34.480
B class is a breeze!

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:35.450
You...!

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:38.540
You haven't been listening to what I said just now.

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:40.570
Have you?

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:43.550
I am going for the B class because I understand.

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:45.210
But, this is...

00:13:45.210 --> 00:13:50.620
B class is for amateurs who have a high record of achievements.

00:13:50.620 --> 00:13:53.310
Do you guys have such a track record, eh!?

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:54.960
Isn't that what you wanted to say!?

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:56.820
By the way...

00:13:59.390 --> 00:14:05.150
I am the newcomer who fought the featherweight Rikiishi Toru, and the bantamweight Wolf Kanagushi.

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:09.440
I splendidly fought each of them to a draw.

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:13.660
You fought Wolf Kanagushi?

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:24.300
Would you happen to be the street boxer that the media was talking about the other day?

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:27.620
Oh, you knew already? I am glad to hear that.

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:30.110
So that means, there shouldn't be any problems.

00:14:30.110 --> 00:14:31.320
What do you say?

00:14:32.310 --> 00:14:36.420
As a matter of fact, I am holding back by going for the B class.

00:14:36.940 --> 00:14:41.040
I was planning to head right into the A class from the very start!

00:14:55.930 --> 00:14:58.330
All right, Number 27, are you ready?

00:14:58.810 --> 00:15:02.150
Okay, okay! We're ready to rumble over here!

00:15:02.150 --> 00:15:03.330
Over there, are you ready?

00:15:07.540 --> 00:15:09.270
Begin sparring!

00:15:09.270 --> 00:15:10.090
Fight!

00:15:10.770 --> 00:15:11.610
Go on!

00:15:11.610 --> 00:15:13.060
Don't lose.

00:15:22.030 --> 00:15:23.940
Wh-What are you doing Nishi, you idiot!

00:15:24.580 --> 00:15:26.530
Hit! Hit, hit!

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:27.930
Hit him back!

00:15:27.930 --> 00:15:28.530
Come on, Nishi!

00:15:29.180 --> 00:15:30.510
Hit him!

00:15:30.510 --> 00:15:32.370
What do you think you're wearing those gloves for, you moron!?

00:15:32.370 --> 00:15:33.820
Hit him back! Return the punches!

00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:36.010
Just hit him already!

00:15:36.010 --> 00:15:37.890
Hit back, dammit!

00:15:37.890 --> 00:15:38.490
Nishi!

00:15:38.490 --> 00:15:41.120
Just shut your trap already, Yabuki-kun.

00:15:41.990 --> 00:15:43.000
What did you say?

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:47.520
Look, your friend hasn't been punched yet.

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:49.010
Look closely!

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:54.410
He's keeping a tight guard and evading his opponent's punches.

00:15:56.910 --> 00:15:57.600
You're right.

00:15:59.240 --> 00:16:03.060
I guess you're more excited than the guy who's fighting.

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:06.810
He'll never win if he keeps running!

00:16:06.810 --> 00:16:09.070
Nishi, don't mind it! Keep going, keep going!

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:09.860
Don't run!

00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:11.360
<i>What kind of man are you?</i>

00:16:11.360 --> 00:16:13.570
He's not really running, you know?

00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:15.070
Wh-What?

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:17.340
He's analysing his opponent's moves.

00:16:17.340 --> 00:16:19.350
You really don't know anything, do you?

00:16:21.220 --> 00:16:24.430
Damn it, you talk too much!

00:16:24.430 --> 00:16:26.090
Now piss off or I'll clobber you!

00:16:26.090 --> 00:16:28.360
Hey, hey, look over there.

00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:30.590
Number 27 has begun his counter.

00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:40.600
That's it, Nishi! Go get him!

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:45.230
Go, go, go! You're almost there!

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:47.110
Get him!

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:50.110
Go! Go! Beat him down!

00:16:54.070 --> 00:16:55.880
Keep it up!

00:16:55.880 --> 00:16:57.790
Hit, hit, hit, hit, hit!

00:16:57.790 --> 00:16:58.880
Hit him!

00:17:05.530 --> 00:17:06.530
All right, separate!

00:17:10.790 --> 00:17:11.880
Hey, hey, hey!

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:14.540
You made me worry!

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:20.680
How did it go? I bet I won by points, didn't I?

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:22.780
You did really well, Nishi.

00:17:23.380 --> 00:17:26.650
You're guaranteed to pass!

00:17:29.550 --> 00:17:31.530
This ends the C class test.

00:17:31.530 --> 00:17:33.910
We will now move on to the B class test.

00:17:33.910 --> 00:17:36.660
First, Number 26 and Number 14!

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:40.880
Yeah, it's me, it's me! Number 26 is me!

00:17:40.880 --> 00:17:44.120
And Number 14 would be me.

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:45.990
Now hurry up and get prepared.

00:17:57.850 --> 00:18:00.810
Oh, this is really awesome. That Number 14 has great footwork!

00:18:00.810 --> 00:18:02.880
You really ended up with a bad matchup...

00:18:04.360 --> 00:18:06.490
Your opponent is the high school champ, isn't he?

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:11.610
All I have to do is beat up this guy and get the B class license.

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:13.820
Don't hold it against me, Inagaki!

00:18:19.560 --> 00:18:22.790
Knock it off, Joe! He's no ordinary guy!

00:18:25.970 --> 00:18:27.580
All the more reason I should be grateful!

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:31.780
If I beat this big shot with one punch, then passing the test will be guaranteed!

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:34.940
Well then, just simmer down and watch!

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:37.540
First round. Start!

00:18:48.890 --> 00:18:51.480
How do you plan on passing like that!?

00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:52.730
What!?

00:19:01.720 --> 00:19:03.810
This is bad. Run, Joe!

00:19:06.420 --> 00:19:07.810
Damn it, you think you're so...

00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:11.460
Oh, no...

00:19:10.360 --> 00:19:11.460
<i>What was that?</i>

00:19:13.320 --> 00:19:14.440
Slip, slip!

00:19:14.440 --> 00:19:15.140
Now stand up!

00:19:15.140 --> 00:19:16.590
D-Damn.

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:18.380
Wipe your gloves!

00:19:18.380 --> 00:19:20.000
You'll pay for that!

00:19:20.850 --> 00:19:21.430
Outta my way!

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:22.510
Damn it.

00:19:32.220 --> 00:19:33.900
Stop, stop!

00:19:34.990 --> 00:19:35.570
Joe!

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:37.350
Ah, this is awful!

00:19:37.350 --> 00:19:39.650
It's only a matter of time before he's KO'd!

00:19:41.550 --> 00:19:44.490
Hold on tight, Joe! Are you all right!?

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:46.580
Joe, you better quit!

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:49.500
There is always next time, so quit now!

00:19:52.840 --> 00:19:54.500
Don't kid me around.

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:56.050
What kind of nonsense is that?

00:19:58.130 --> 00:19:59.730
I have no choice.

00:19:59.730 --> 00:20:01.880
I'll show them all my trump card.

00:20:04.210 --> 00:20:05.380
Trump card?

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:08.140
What do you mean, trump card?

00:20:08.540 --> 00:20:09.790
You just wait and see.

00:20:11.800 --> 00:20:13.060
Last round!

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:36.640
D-Damn.

00:20:36.640 --> 00:20:38.030
Is he making fun of me?

00:20:43.390 --> 00:20:46.460
Huh? Is he throwing the match already?

00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:47.720
Lookin' like a scarecrow!

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:49.390
It's like he's begging to get a beating already!

00:20:52.110 --> 00:20:54.400
It's like he's saying, "Come and hit me"!

00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:56.110
Go, go, hit him!

00:20:56.110 --> 00:20:57.760
He's just bluffing!

00:20:58.790 --> 00:21:00.000
Go get him!

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.360
Go, go!

00:21:03.630 --> 00:21:05.770
I won't hold back, Yabuki-san!

00:21:19.050 --> 00:21:20.760
I've been waiting for this!

00:21:23.790 --> 00:21:24.550
Shit!

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:49.740
Ah... stop them! Make them stop!

00:21:49.740 --> 00:21:50.790
Rope down!

00:21:50.790 --> 00:21:53.730
Stop! Stop! Rope down!

00:21:54.790 --> 00:21:55.790
Shut up, dumbass!

00:22:05.300 --> 00:22:07.300
Don't run away, you bastard!

00:22:09.470 --> 00:22:10.350
Please help me!

00:22:10.350 --> 00:22:11.140
Wait!

00:22:13.420 --> 00:22:14.310
Please save me!

00:22:14.310 --> 00:22:15.270
Sav--

00:22:17.640 --> 00:22:19.900
Please stop! Please stop!

00:22:20.610 --> 00:22:21.900
Joe!

00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:23.480
H-Hey, stop, stop!

00:22:23.480 --> 00:22:26.320
This isn't a fight! Stop! Stop now!

00:22:38.210 --> 00:22:39.640
Hey, referee, what's wrong?

00:22:39.640 --> 00:22:41.380
Start the count!

00:22:43.380 --> 00:22:47.290
Joe, are you insane? You did something terrible!

00:22:47.290 --> 00:22:50.030
You even chased him out of the ring and continued hitting him!

00:22:58.000 --> 00:22:59.600
I think I killed him...

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:01.740
What do you mean, you think you killed him?

00:23:01.740 --> 00:23:03.610
What are you going to do!?

00:23:03.610 --> 00:23:06.540
It's too late for that now, I've already done it...

00:23:08.660 --> 00:23:11.160
Hey, Inagaki. Please forgive me.

00:23:12.220 --> 00:23:14.910
But... this looks awful.

00:23:17.160 --> 00:23:19.110
This... really is bad...

00:23:43.710 --> 00:23:46.140
Joe went wild in the crucial pro test.

00:23:46.140 --> 00:23:49.230
But he managed to pass it the second time around.

00:23:49.230 --> 00:23:55.970
He gives hope to the people in the slums, and with his opponent decided, he awakens as a boxer.

00:23:55.970 --> 00:24:00.920
Light a fire on the Bridge of Tears! Now, for Joe, who sets out as a pro boxer...

00:24:00.920 --> 00:24:02.520
Which way is tomorrow!?
